    "answer": "Yes. Per ADR-010 (amended 2026-10-02), context evals are a nightly GitHub Actions job. It asks lore-api to write a question from each sampled document, assemble the context, and judge the answer (#2443). The older nightly `eval_runner` and `context_core_builder` jobs, and the weekly `autoresearch` job, were deleted on 2026-10-02. The new job keeps no stored baseline. Developers can also run the evals by hand with `node scripts/context-evals/run.mjs` against lore-api. I did not open the workflow file, so I haven't confirmed the actual cron schedule.",
